.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle gum"
copies optional Wattle modules into a project.
These modules are known as
.Em Gum
and are installed in
.Eo
.Pa share/wattle/src/gum/
.Ec
under
.Ql "*prefix*" .
.Ic g
is a synonym for
.Cm gum .
.Pp
With no module names,
the command lists each available module and its description
in two columns.
Descriptions are wrapped in the same way as
.Fl "-help"
output.
.Pp
With one or more module names,
the command copies each module’s source and licence into a
.Eo
.Pa gum/
.Ec
subdirectory under
.Ar directory .
It prints
.Ql "copied"
or
.Ql "unchanged"
followed by the path of each file.
The default destination is
.Eo
.Pa deps/gum/
.Ec .
A project imports a copy by its relative path,
as in
.Ql "\*(lpimport \&./deps/gum/args :as args\*(rp" .
.Pp
A build made without the OS library does not include
.Cm gum .
The command reports this limitation and exits with status 1.
.Pp
The command checks all module names and destinations before copying
any files.
An unknown module name or a destination file with different
content causes it to exit with status 1 without copying files.
A destination file with the same content is left unchanged.
.Fl "-force"
permits replacement of files with different content.
.
